# ---- host_dma (BCM2835 DMA engine) — NO QEMU test, by platform limit ----
# src/host/host_dma.rs (UART/MAI/SD-TX CB-chain arming) is #![cfg(nh_real_hw)]
# (no-semihost + platform-raspi3b) and is therefore not even compiled
# into the QEMU guest-test build (default = semihost). Beyond the cfg,
# QEMU raspi3b's BCM2835 DMA model (hw/dma/bcm2835_dma.c, QEMU 10.1.1)
# cannot exercise the path faithfully:
#   - It IGNORES DREQ / TI.PERMAP peripheral flow-control entirely
#     (bcm2835_dma_update copies at full speed), so the DREQ-paced
#     UART-TX / SD FIFO feed host_dma arms is not modelled.
#   - A write to a peripheral FIFO via the bus alias is a plain
#     stl_le_phys memory store; QEMU does not deliver DMA'd bytes to the
#     PL011 transmit path the way real silicon does, so "DMA a string,
#     observe it on the wire" has nothing to observe.
# (The CB-chain walk, CONBLK_AD advance, gpu_bus_mr 0xC0000000/0x7E000000
# alias, and CS.INT/END completion IRQ ARE modelled — the gaps above are
# the DREQ pacing and peripheral-FIFO delivery, exactly the parts a
# UART-TX-DMA completion test would assert.)
# Documented validation route: the sd-probe hardware probe
# (src/host/sd/probe.rs, built with `--features "pi-bare-metal sd-probe"`,
# run on a real Pi Zero 2 W) exercises host_dma's CB-chain arming via
# the SD-TX channel (write_block_dma -> arm_sd_tx) AND a dedicated
# RAM-to-RAM self-check on the same channel
# (host_dma::sd_tx_dma_selfcheck — the UART-TX channel is off limits
# for the check, since it is live as the console backend by probe
# time). See docs/SD_DMA_AUTOSAVE.md and the sd-probe write-up.
